  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Notifications
  </title>
  <p>
    Notifications are brief messages from applications or the desktop, such as new-message
    alerts or low-battery warnings. Orca keeps recent notifications it receives so you can
    review an announcement you missed or interrupted.
  </p>
  <section id="reviewing-messages">
    <title>Reviewing messages</title>
    <p>
      Use the last notification command to return to the most recent message. The previous and
      next commands move through older and newer messages. Each command also reports how long
      ago the message was received.
    </p>
    <section id="commands-reviewing-messages">
      <title>Commands</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Notification presenter</gui> group.
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Present last notification message</gui>
            Unbound by default.
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Present previous notification message</gui>
            Unbound by default.
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Present next notification message</gui>
            Unbound by default.
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Present notification messages list</gui>
            Unbound by default.
          </p>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </section>
  <section id="notification-list">
    <title>Notification list</title>
    <p>
      The notification messages list shows recent messages, newest first, alongside how long ago
      each was received. Use <key>Up Arrow</key> and <key>Down Arrow</key> to move through the messages.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use Clear to remove the notification history and close the list. Use Close to dismiss the
      list without clearing it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The history contains notifications received by Orca during the current session and is
      cleared when Orca restarts.
    </p>
  </section>
